TITLE:: RCSubseqLibrary
summary:: The vocabulary of subsequences of a piece
categories:: Libraries>reCurrent
related:: Classes/RCRhythmDict, Classes/RCSubseq

DESCRIPTION::
Entries are nested Events: category → sub-category → name → code::[name, shift, durs, params?, keysIgnoreOrder?]::, addressed by dotted paths.

CLASSMETHODS::
METHOD:: newFrom
argument:: nestedEvent

INSTANCEMETHODS::
METHOD:: at
argument:: name
returns:: the entry padded to 4 elements, or nil with an error
METHOD:: put
argument:: category
argument:: event
METHOD:: includes
METHOD:: size
argument:: name
METHOD:: names
METHOD:: entries

EXAMPLES::
code::
~lib = RCSubseqLibrary.newFrom((
    clave_44: (son: ('1': [\son, 0, [3, 3, 4, 2, 4]])),
    percs: (kick: (fourfour: [\fourfour, 0, [1, 1, 1, 1]]))
));
~lib.at("percs.kick.fourfour");
::
